@startuml roles_workflow_pattern_b

title Pattern B: Separated Workflow (Generic Converter)

participant "Vendor Files" as vendor
participant "Data Converter" as converter
participant "AnnData +\ngeneric_semantics" as adata_generic
participant "Metadata Writer\n(exploreDE)" as writer1
participant "Metadata Writer\n(prolfqua)" as writer2
participant "AnnData\n(complete)" as adata_complete
participant "Applications" as apps

vendor -> converter : Parse
activate converter

converter -> adata_generic : Create X, layers, obs, var
converter -> adata_generic : Create uns['generic_semantics']\n(REQUIRED in this pattern)

note right of converter
  Data Converter knows:
  • Vendor format

  Does NOT know:
  • Which applications will be used

  Documents semantics for
  downstream users
end note

deactivate converter

adata_generic -> writer1 : Reads generic_semantics
activate writer1
writer1 -> adata_generic : Create uns['exploreDE']['column_roles']
deactivate writer1

adata_generic -> writer2 : Reads generic_semantics
activate writer2
writer2 -> adata_complete : Create uns['prolfqua']['column_roles']
deactivate writer2

note over writer1, writer2
  Metadata Writers know:
  • Application specifications
  • Generic semantics vocabulary

  Do NOT need to know:
  • Vendor format details
end note

adata_complete -> apps : Ready for multiple applications

@enduml

